<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/assertion> {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-ddi> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-ddi> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Turing diffusion-driven instability" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-ddi> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A homogeneous steady state of two reacting chemicals that is stable without diffusion can become unstable to spatial perturbations when the chemicals diffuse at different rates, spontaneously producing a pattern." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-ddi> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/TestableHypothesis> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-ddi> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "u_t = f(u,v) + D_u \\nabla^2 u, v_t = g(u,v) + D_v \\nabla^2 v; with tr J < 0 and det J > 0, instability at some wavenumber k iff D_v f_u + D_u g_v > 2\\sqrt{D_u D_v \\det J}, which requires D_u \\ne D_v" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-ddi> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Assumptions: two species, smooth kinetics, linearization about a homogeneous steady state, fixed domain without growth or mechanics. Formal status: the linear instability conditions are proved; existence and stability of nonlinear patterns are proved for many specific models but not in general." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-ddi> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/proposedTest> "Measure the reaction Jacobian and the diffusivities of a candidate morphogen pair independently, check that the inequality holds, and then confirm that perturbing the diffusivity ratio switches patterning on or off." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-ddi> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hypothesisType> "model-theorem" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-ddi> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Alan Turing (1952) The chemical basis of morphogenesis" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/turing-ddi> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.64.2953> .
}
